@startuml
title BerSU Ball - Logical Model

start
:Receive two lists of skills;
:Sort both lists ascending;
:Call max_pairs(Boys, Girls, Pairs);

while (Both lists are non-empty?) is (yes)
  :Compare heads B and G;

  if (abs(B - G) <= 1?) then (yes)
    :Count one pair;
    :Consume both heads;
  else (no)
    if (B < G - 1?) then (yes)
      :Consume boy head;
    else (no)
      :Consume girl head;
    endif
  endif
endwhile (no)

:Return total pairs;
stop

legend right
  The diagram follows the same greedy logic used in the Prolog predicate.
  Each decision reduces one of the lists, which guarantees linear traversal
  after sorting.
endlegend

@enduml